<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Sprint 0 — Project Charter</title><!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View><w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]--><style>@page{size:21cm 29.7cm;margin:2.5cm 2.2cm;mso-header-margin:1cm;mso-footer-margin:1cm;}body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.4;}h1{font-size:19pt;color:#0d2b45;border-bottom:3px solid #1f7a8c;padding-bottom:5pt;margin:0 0 6pt;}h2{font-size:14pt;color:#0d2b45;border-bottom:1px solid #9db8cc;padding-bottom:3pt;margin:20pt 0 6pt;page-break-after:avoid;}h3{font-size:12pt;color:#1f7a8c;margin:12pt 0 4pt;page-break-after:avoid;}p{margin:0 0 7pt;text-align:justify;}.es{color:#3d4c5c;font-style:italic;border-left:2pt solid #c0392b;padding-left:8pt;}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:6pt 0 12pt;}td,th{border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;}th{background:#12324a;color:#fff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;text-align:left;}.cover{text-align:center;}.cover .inst{font-size:13pt;font-weight:bold;color:#0d2b45;letter-spacing:1pt;}.cover .big{font-size:24pt;font-weight:bold;color:#12324a;margin:22pt 0 4pt;}.cover .sub{font-size:13pt;color:#1f7a8c;}.pb{page-break-before:always;}.mono{font-family:Consolas,"Courier New",monospace;font-size:9.5pt;}.hint{color:#8a94a0;font-style:italic;font-size:9.5pt;}.box{border:1px solid #9db8cc;background:#f2f7fb;padding:8pt 10pt;margin:8pt 0;}ul,ol{margin:0 0 8pt 18pt;}li{margin-bottom:3pt;}</style></head><body><div class="cover"><p class="inst">INSTITUTO NACIONAL DE EDUCACIÓN LOURDES — INDEL</p><p>Bachillerato Técnico Vocacional en Desarrollo de Software</p><p>Module 3.6 — English for IT Systems</p><p class="big">SPRINT 0<br>PROJECT CHARTER</p><p class="sub">Activity 04 — Build It in English · Day 1</p><p class="es">Acta de arranque del proyecto · Actividad 04 · Día 1</p><br><table style="width:82%;margin:0 auto"><tr><th style="width:38%">Students / Estudiantes</th><td>Néstor Eduardo Deodanes Martínez · Samuel Mendoza · Marcela Mata · Daniela Rodríguez</td></tr><tr><th>Grade and section / Grado y sección</th><td>3rd Year — BTV Software Development, Section ____</td></tr><tr><th>Project / Proyecto</th><td>Code Metrics Lab — Text &amp; Code Analyser</td></tr><tr><th>Environment / Entorno</th><td>Vue 3 (CDN mode) · HTML / CSS · runs in the browser, no build step</td></tr><tr><th>IDE and version</th><td>Visual Studio Code + Live Server extension (v ____)</td></tr><tr><th>Date / Fecha</th><td>2026-09-02</td></tr><tr><th>Teacher / Docente</th><td>Ing. Javier Arturo García Mineros</td></tr></table></div><div class="pb"></div><h1>1. Purpose of the application</h1><p>Code Metrics Lab is a single-page toolbox that analyses any text or code the user pastes, entirely in the browser, with no server, no database and no build step. It gives instant metrics — word, character, line and paragraph counts and estimated reading time — plus practical utilities: a case converter, a duplicate line finder, a password strength meter with explained criteria, and a JSON formatter and validator. Everything is reactive: results update live as the user types, powered by Vue 3 loaded from a CDN with a local fallback copy for offline use.</p><p class="es">Code Metrics Lab es una caja de herramientas de una sola página que analiza cualquier texto o código que el usuario pegue, completamente en el navegador, sin servidor, sin base de datos y sin proceso de compilación. Ofrece métricas instantáneas — palabras, caracteres, líneas, párrafos y tiempo de lectura — y utilidades: convertidor de mayúsculas/minúsculas, buscador de líneas duplicadas, medidor de fortaleza de contraseñas con criterios explicados, y formateador y validador de JSON. Todo es reactivo: los resultados se actualizan en vivo mientras el usuario escribe, con Vue 3 cargado desde CDN y una copia local de respaldo para uso sin conexión.</p><h1>2. User stories</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">#</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">AS A … I WANT … SO THAT …</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">1</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a developer, I want live counts of words, characters, lines and paragraphs, so that I can measure any text without leaving the page.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• Counters update on every keystroke, no button.<br>• Empty input shows 0 in every counter.<br>• A paragraph is a block separated by one or more blank lines.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">2</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a content writer, I want an estimated reading time, so that I know how long my text takes to read before publishing it.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• Estimate based on 200 words per minute.<br>• Texts under one minute show "&lt; 1 min".<br>• Updates live with the word count.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">3</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a developer, I want to convert text to UPPERCASE, lowercase, Title Case, snake_case and camelCase, so that I can rename identifiers and headings quickly.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• All five conversions shown at once.<br>• Original text is not modified.<br>• snake_case / camelCase remove spaces and punctuation, line by line.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">4</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As an editor, I want to find duplicate lines, so that I can clean repeated content before delivering it.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• Each duplicated line listed with its occurrence count.<br>• Leading/trailing spaces ignored when comparing.<br>• Shows "No duplicate lines found" when clean.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">5</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a user, I want a password strength meter with explained criteria, so that I understand why my password is weak or strong.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• Checks length &ge; 8, uppercase, lowercase, digit, symbol.<br>• Each criterion shown as passed or failed.<br>• Global label Weak / Medium / Strong by criteria met.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">6</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">As a developer, I want to format and validate JSON, so that I can fix configuration files without external tools.</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">• Valid JSON pretty-printed with 2-space indent.<br>• Invalid JSON shows a clear error with position.<br>• Empty input shows a neutral hint, not an error.</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>3. Screens and controls</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">SCREEN OR VIEW</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">CONTROLS (NAMED IN ENGLISH)</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">WHAT THE USER DOES THERE</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Main page — tool selector</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">btnCounterTool · btnCaseTool · btnDuplicatesTool · btnPasswordTool · btnJsonTool</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Chooses which analysis tool is active; active button is highlighted.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Main page — editor area</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">txtSourceText (textarea) · lblEditorHint</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Types or pastes the text, code, password or JSON to analyse.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Main page — live results</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">pnlResults · lblWordCount · lblCharCount · lblLineCount · lblParagraphCount · lblReadingTime</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Reads live metrics that update on every keystroke.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Results — tool outputs</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">txtUpperResult · txtLowerResult · txtTitleResult · txtSnakeResult · txtCamelResult · lstDuplicateLines · prgPasswordStrength · lstPasswordCriteria · txtJsonOutput · lblErrorMessage · lblEmptyState</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Reads the active tool output: converted text, duplicate report, strength criteria, formatted JSON or error.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="pb"></div><h1>4. Data model</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">CLASS</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">FIELDS AND TYPES</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">WHERE THE DATA LIVES (MEMORY / FILE)</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">AppState (Vue reactive state)</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">sourceText: String · activeTool: String ('counter' | 'case' | 'duplicates' | 'password' | 'json')</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Memory (Vue reactive object). Reset on reload.</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">results (computed properties)</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">wordCount, charCount, lineCount, paragraphCount: Number · readingTime: String · caseResults: Object · duplicateLines: Array · passwordCriteria: Array · formattedJson: String · jsonError: String</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Memory — derived from sourceText and activeTool; never stored.</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>5. Setup log</h1><table class="wt"><tbody><tr><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">STEP</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">COMMAND OR ACTION</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">RESULT</th><th style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;background:#12324a;color:#ffffff;font-weight:bold;font-size:9pt;">PROBLEM FOUND AND HOW YOU SOLVED IT</th></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Install / verify SDK</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Install VS Code and the Live Server extension</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">VS Code opens; Live Server shown in the status bar</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Live Server not installed by default — added from Extensions (Ctrl+Shift+X).</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Crear proyecto</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Create folder CodeMetricsLab with index.html, /css, /js, /assets</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Folder structure created, all names in English</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">________ (write the real problem, or "No problem")</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Primera etapa</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Right-click index.html → "Open with Live Server"</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Page opens at http://127.0.0.1:5500 with no console errors — EV-01</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">________ (write the real problem, or "No problem")</td></tr><tr><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Estructura de carpetas</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Reference Vue 3 from unpkg CDN and keep a local copy in /assets</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">vue.global.prod.js available locally for offline use</td><td style="border:1px solid #7f9db9;padding:4pt 6pt;vertical-align:top;font-size:9.5pt;">Lab internet unreliable — kept a local fallback so the app runs offline.</td></tr></tbody></table><h1>6. Risks</h1><p>1) The lab may have no internet, breaking the Vue CDN reference — mitigated with a local copy of vue.global.prod.js in /assets loaded as a fallback. 2) Four people share the work, so versions could get mixed — mitigated with dated backups after every block and both names on every file. 3) Spanish identifiers or messages could slip into the code and get the work rejected — mitigated with a peer-review checklist before every backup. 4) The JSON validator could crash on bad input — mitigated by wrapping JSON.parse in try/catch with a controlled error message.</p><p class="es">1) El laboratorio puede quedarse sin internet y romper la referencia CDN de Vue — se mitiga con una copia local de vue.global.prod.js en /assets cargada como respaldo. 2) Cuatro personas comparten el trabajo y las versiones podrían mezclarse — se mitiga con respaldos fechados tras cada bloque y los nombres en cada archivo. 3) Identificadores o mensajes en español podrían colarse y provocar el rechazo — se mitiga con una lista de revisión entre compañeros antes de cada respaldo. 4) El validador JSON podría fallar con entradas inválidas — se mitiga con try/catch y un mensaje de error controlado.</p><div class="box"><b>Evidence:</b> attach screenshot EV-01 showing the empty project running, and the content of your README.md file.<br><span class="es">Adjunte la captura EV-01 con el proyecto vacío en ejecución y el contenido de su README.md.</span></div><br><br><table style="width:100%"><tr>
